# HirForwardDecl — typed forwarding metadata (C2 / M4 first slice, 2026-08-07).
#
# doc/03_plan/compiler/forwarding/zero_cost_layers_c0_c5_staged_implementation_plan_2026-08-07.md
# M4 (= C2): "HirForwardDecl emission, phase-by-phase retirement of
# src/app/desugar/forwarding.spl." That plan explicitly flags the full
# compiler-pass sequence (resolve layer DAG -> prove layer-eq views ->
# transitive forwarding graph -> join-point IDs -> weave static aspects ->
# specialize service table -> collapse chains -> erase identity views ->
# devirtualize -> inline/SROA -> verify effects -> lower one physical call) as
# multi-week scope, not a single bounded slice.
#
# This file is ONLY the data-structure shape from
# doc/05_design/language/forwarding/layer_forwarding_and_layer_eq_types.md §4,
# matching M0's own "decisive first milestone, zero runtime effect" precedent
# (see layer_dag_checker.spl / layer_eq_checker.spl for the established
# pattern: a self-contained struct + proof/accessor helpers + spec, not wired
# into any compiler pass yet).
#
# Deliberately NOT wired into anything:
#   - NOT added to hir_definitions.spl's HirFunction/HirClass/etc. node union,
#     so it cannot reach the MIR default-arm dispatch
#     (50.mir/_MirLoweringExpr/expr_dispatch.spl:3380, documented as "loud" —
#     any new HIR kind without an arm fails compilation, so staying off that
#     union is what keeps this a zero-risk addition).
#   - NOT consumed by src/app/desugar/forwarding.spl (out of scope for this
#     slice; that file is untouched).
#   - NOT registered with any driver/pipeline pass.
#
# Field-for-field match with the design doc's sketch:
#   logical_symbol        - the forwarding declaration's own logical name
#   receiver_projection   - field path from receiver to the forwarding target,
#                            e.g. "draw" for `alias fn foo = draw.foo`
#   target_symbol          - the physical symbol ultimately being forwarded to
#   layer_view_map          - index into the proven layer-eq view table
#                            (see layer_eq_checker.spl; table itself is future
#                            work, hence u32 index rather than an embedded
#                            LayerEqType)
#   effect_summary          - index/bitset placeholder for the effect-verifier
#                            summary (see effect_verifier.spl, M6 wiring)
#   logical_join_point_id    - stable ID that AOP advice (M5) targets so a
#                            business-logic-free wrapper need not exist
#                            physically

struct HirForwardDecl:
    """Typed forwarding metadata: one logical-to-physical forwarding site.

    First slice: data shape only. No pass reads or writes this type yet.
    """
    logical_symbol: text
    receiver_projection: text
    target_symbol: text
    layer_view_map: u32
    effect_summary: u32
    logical_join_point_id: u32

export HirForwardDecl
